++# Classic PDF Parity Evidence Report
++
++**Date:** 2026-01-25  
++**Status:** Time basis mapping implemented correctly; reveals fundamental physics accuracy gap
++
++---
++
++## Executive Summary
++
++The PDF parity comparison logic has been **fixed and is working correctly**. The time basis mapping automatically selects the appropriate mode (absolute vs ET) per case using MAE-based anchor fitting. However, the tests reveal that the simulation produces times **1-10 seconds slower** than PDF ground truth, indicating a **physics accuracy issue** rather than a time basis alignment problem.
++
++---
++
++## Implementation Completed
++
++### 1. Power Mode Regression Guard ✅
++- Created `classic_sim_runner_power_mode.spec.ts` to prevent regressions
++- Verifies QuarterPro/BonnevillePro use `engine.hpCurve` (NOT `powerHP`)
++- Verifies QuarterJr uses `powerHP` (NOT `engine.hpCurve`)
++- **All 3 tests passing**
++
++### 2. Time Basis Mapping ✅
++- Implemented RMS-based mode selection using anchor distances (>=60ft)
++- Two modes tested per case:
++  - **Mode A (as_et)**: PDF time_et_s used directly
++  - **Mode B (abs_minus_offset)**: PDF time_et_s - rollout_offset
++- Selects mode with lower Mean Absolute Error at anchors (330, 660, 1000, 1320ft)
++- Skips rollout/staged rows from comparisons (they use dual-time format)
++
++### 3. Parity Diagnostics ✅
++- Per-model bucket statistics (60-330ft, 330-660ft, 660-1000ft, 1000-finish)
++- Reports: count, mean ET delta, P95 ET delta, mean MPH delta, P95 MPH delta
++- Worst 10 ET deltas per model
++- Time mapping summary (mode, offset, MAE per case)
++
++---
++
++## Evidence: QuarterPro Parity Results
++
