++## ✅ Deliverable 2: EarliestMismatchFinder
++
++**Status**: COMPLETE
++
++**File**: `src/integration-tests/helpers/earliest_mismatch_finder.ts`
++
++### What It Does
++Identifies the first checkpoint that fails tolerance using VB6 print formatting rules:
++- **Time**: 2 decimals (except rollout)
++- **MPH**: 1 decimal
++- **Accel**: 2 decimals
++- **RPM**: Nearest 10
++
++### Key Functions
++
++**`findEarliestMismatch()`**
++- Takes expected JSON checkpoints + actual timeslipRows
++- Applies VB6 formatting to both
++- Returns first checkpoint that fails tolerance
++- Deterministic (same result every run)
++
++**`applyVB6Formatting()`**
++```typescript
++{
++  time_s: Math.round(time * 100) / 100,      // 2 decimals
++  mph: Math.round(mph * 10) / 10,            // 1 decimal
++  accel_g: Math.round(accel * 100) / 100,    // 2 decimals
++  rpm: Math.round(rpm / 10) * 10,            // Nearest 10
++}
++```
++
++**`getDefaultTolerance()`**
++- ProStock: ±0.01s, ±0.5mph, ±0.05g, ±50rpm
++- Quarter Pro/Jr: ±0.30s, ±4.0mph, ±0.50g, ±500rpm
++
++### Return Type
++```typescript
++interface MismatchInfo {
++  checkpoint: string;
++  distance_ft: number | null;
++  expected: FormattedCheckpoint;
++  actual: FormattedCheckpoint;
++  deltas: { time_s, mph, accel_g, rpm, gear };
++  failedFields: string[];
++}
++```
