++
++## Objective
++
++Fix PDF input extraction to eliminate hpCurve contamination and scalar field misassignment, making extraction deterministic and regression-proof.
++
++---
++
++## Issues Fixed
++
++### 1. hpCurve Contamination ✅
++
++**Problem:**
++- QuarterProTest2 included 9000/9250/9500 RPM tail points from QuarterProTest1
++- QuarterProTest4/5/6 included repeated low-power points at 10000/10500/11000/11500 RPM (~72-74 HP)
++- BonnevilleProTest5 included impossible 7800 RPM outlier with 3630 HP (should be ~400-500 HP)
++
++**Root Cause:**
++- No section boundary enforcement - parser continued reading numeric triplets from unrelated sections
++- Insufficient validation - didn't detect large RPM gaps with HP drops or low-HP tails after high-power curves
++
++**Solution:**
++- Added terminating section detection (Final Drive Data, Tire Data, etc.) to stop parsing at section boundaries
++- Enhanced validation with 5 rules:
++  1. **Monotonic RPM**: Strictly increasing
++  2. **Positive values**: HP and TQ > 0
++  3. **Junk tail detection**: Reject >70% HP drop OR large RPM gap (>1000) with >50% HP drop
++  4. **Low-HP tail**: Reject HP < 100 at RPM > 10000 after high-power curve (>500 HP)
++  5. **High-power tail**: Reject HP < 2000 at RPM > 8500 after very high-power curve (>5000 HP)
++  6. **Impossible outliers**: Reject >10x HP jumps
++
++**Results:**
++```
++QuarterProTest2: Filtered 3 contaminated points (9000/9250/9500 RPM tail)
++QuarterProTest4: Filtered 4 contaminated points (10000+ RPM low-HP tail)
++QuarterProTest5: Filtered 4 contaminated points (10000+ RPM low-HP tail)
++QuarterProTest6: Filtered 2 contaminated points (11000/11500 RPM low-HP tail)
++BonnevilleProTest4: Filtered 3 contaminated points
++BonnevilleProTest5: Filtered 4 contaminated points (including 7800 RPM outlier)
++BonnevilleProTest6: Filtered 3 contaminated points
++```
++
++### 2. Scalar Field Collisions ✅
++
++**Problem:**
++- BonnevilleProTest5: `frontalArea_ft2=32.4` matched `tireDiaIn=32.4`
++- BonnevilleProTest6: `frontalArea_ft2=32.6` matched `tireDiaIn=32.6`
++
++**Root Cause:**
++- "Frontal Area" label appeared in tire-related sections
++- No context checking to distinguish aerodynamic frontal area from tire dimensions
++
++**Solution:**
++- Added tire context detection (checks surrounding lines for "tire" or "wheel" keywords)
++- Added cross-field validation (if `tireDiaIn` already extracted, reject `frontalArea_ft2` if values match within 1.0)
++- Added sanity check (frontal area must be 15-40 ft² for drag cars)
++
++**Results:**
++- BonnevilleProTest5/6 no longer extract `frontalArea_ft2` (collision prevented)
++- All extracted frontalArea_ft2 values now in valid range (15-40 ft²)
