++# JSON Physics Parity Test Status
++
++**Date:** 2025-01-27  
++**Status:** ⚠️ Infrastructure complete, critical field loss identified in normalization pipeline
++
++---
++
++## Summary
++
++I've implemented a comprehensive JSON→ClassicRawInputs→normalization→simulation pathway to validate physics parity. The test infrastructure is complete and working, but it reveals a **critical architectural issue**: the `ClassicEffectiveInputs` type only preserves 6 fields, causing massive field loss during normalization.
++
++---
++
++## ✅ Deliverables Complete
++
++### 1. Extended ClassicRawInputs Type
++**`src/integration-tests/helpers/classic_types.ts`**
++- Extended from 16 fields to **60+ fields**
++- Now supports all JSON fields:
++  - Vehicle: weightLb, wheelbaseIn, overhangIn
++  - Tires: tireDiaIn, tireRolloutIn, tireWidthIn
++  - Drivetrain: rearGear, drivetrainEfficiency, drivetrainMode
++  - Transmission: transmissionGearing[], shiftRpm
++  - Converter: stallRpm, converterDiameterIn
++  - Clutch: launchRpm, slipRpm, clutchSlippage
++  - Aero: frontalArea_ft2, dragCoeff, liftCoeff
++  - PMI: engineFlywheelClutchPMI, transmissionDriveshaftPMI, tiresWheelsRingGearPMI
++  - Environment: elevation, barometerInHg, temperatureF, humidityPct, tractionIndex, windVelocityMph, windAngleDeg, trackTempF
++  - Power: powerHP, peakHPRPM, hpCurve, hpTorqueMultiplier
++
++### 2. Comprehensive JSON→ClassicRawInputs Mapper
++**`src/integration-tests/helpers/json_to_classic_raw.ts`** (268 lines)
++- Maps **all** JSON fields to ClassicRawInputs
++- Preserves transmission gearing arrays
++- Preserves rotational inertia (PMI) values
++- Preserves environment fields including traction index
++- Preserves aero fields (frontalArea_ft2, dragCoeff, liftCoeff)
++- No field renaming mistakes
++- Tracks extracted fields for debugging
++
++### 3. JSON Physics Parity Test
++**`src/integration-tests/classic_json_physics_parity.spec.ts`** (358 lines)
++- Uses ClassicRawInputs → normalization → simulation pathway
