++   - Better than QuarterJr but still significant
++   - Time deltas small (avg ~0.06s)
++   - MPH deltas moderate (avg ~1.1 mph, max ~3.2 mph)
++   - Suggests clutch slip behavior differs slightly
++
++### Possible Causes
++
++1. **Converter/Clutch Physics**:
++   - VB6Exact may use different slip ratios, lockup logic, or torque multiplication
++   - QuarterJr shows 2x RPM difference → converter behavior significantly different
++
++2. **Shift Logic**:
++   - Gear mismatches in QuarterJr (19 mismatches)
++   - Shift points may be calculated differently
++
++3. **Traction Model**:
++   - Even with traction index passed, the traction curve application may differ
++   - Launch acceleration and tire slip may use different formulas
++
++4. **Missing Parameters**:
++   - Some VB6-specific parameters may not be mapped
++   - Converter diameter, clutch slippage ratios, etc. may need tuning
++
++5. **Numerical Integration**:
++   - Time step size, integration method, or rounding may differ
++   - VB6 uses Float32 (Single), but integration logic may vary
