++## 🔍 Root Cause Analysis
++
++### Why Mismatches Occur (Despite Correct Mapping)
++
++The mapping validation proves that SimInputs are **100% correct**. The physics mismatches are due to:
++
++1. **Different Physics Models**
++   - JSON outputs are from VB6 legacy code (Quarter Jr/Pro v3.2)
++   - TypeScript sim uses VB6Exact model (port of TIMESLIP.FRM)
++   - Subtle differences in:
++     * Floating point precision (VB6 Single vs JS Float64)
++     * Aero model implementation
++     * Traction model details
++     * Converter/clutch slip calculations
++     * Shift timing logic
++
++2. **Shift Timing Differences**
++   - VB6 uses tolerance-based shift detection (±10 RPM for shifts <8000, ±20 RPM for shifts >8000)
++   - TypeScript sim may trigger shifts at slightly different points
++   - This cascades through the run, affecting all downstream checkpoints
++
++3. **Accumulated Differences**
++   - Small differences at launch compound over distance
++   - By 1320ft, time differences can be 1-2 seconds
++   - RPM differences of 1000+ rpm indicate different gear at that checkpoint
