++## 🎓 Key Learnings
++
++### 1. VB6 Truth is Non-Negotiable
++- Intermediate checkpoints (21ft, 50ft, 59ft) are from **time triggers**, not distance triggers
++- VB6 has exactly 8 distance triggers for Quarter Jr/Pro: `[30, 60, 330, 594, 660, 1000, 1254, 1320]`
++- 594ft and 1254ft are skipped unless ShiftFlag=2 (post-shift)
++
++### 2. Trigger Priority Matters
++- VB6 selects EARLIEST event when multiple triggers fire in one step
++- Priority is determined by comparing interpolated velocities (smallest wins)
++- Our implementation sorts by distance (equivalent for monotonic acceleration)
++
++### 3. Provenance Schema Must Be Strict
++```typescript
++interface TriggerDebugInfo {
++  triggerKind: 'distance' | 'time' | 'speed' | 'shift' | 'staged' | 'rollout';
++  triggerTarget: number | null;
++  interp: {
++    method: 'sub310_distance' | 'sub315_time' | 'velocity_match' | ...;
++    factor1: number;
++    factor2: number;
++    prev: { t, d, v, rpm, gear, accel };
++    curr: { t, d, v, rpm, gear, accel };
++  };
++}
++```
++
++### 4. Bonneville Pro is Different
++- 7 track-specific distance configurations
++- Speed triggers vary by track (60/100 or 100/200 mph)
++- Must use config-based API to specify track type
