++# VB6 Parity Report
++
++This document tracks the progress of achieving exact parity between the TypeScript simulation and the VB6 reference implementation.
++
++## Methodology
++
++**VB6 is the spec.** All physics, trigger schedules, and output formatting must match VB6 exactly. No hardcoding, no fixture adjustments, no tolerance loosening.
++
++### First-Divergence Pipeline
++
++1. **TS Step Trace**: Captures simulation state at each converged velocity step
++2. **VB6 Step Trace**: Instrumented VB6 outputs matching trace format
++3. **Diff Tool**: Finds first step where any field diverges beyond tolerance
++4. **Fix**: Port exact VB6 formula to TS, cite VB6 file+line
++5. **Iterate**: Re-run diff until parity achieved
++
++## Current Status
++
++### Test Results (as of 2026-01-30)
++
++```
++vb6.parity tests: 14 passed, 3 skipped (17 total)
++vb6_equivalence tests: 2 passed (2 total)
++```
++
++### Resolved Issues
++
++| Case | Issue | Resolution |
++|------|-------|------------|
++| QuarterProTest1 | Distance decreased at row 23: 695.0ft -> 692.0ft | Fixed trigger ordering |
++| QuarterJrTest1 | Passes equivalence test | Working |
++
++### Trigger Ordering Bug (FIXED)
++
++**Root Cause**: The shift handling in `vb6_detailed_params_emitter.ts` returned early after emitting shift rows, preventing time triggers from being checked during shifts. This caused a shift-post row at 695ft/4.51s to be emitted BEFORE a time trigger at 692ft/4.50s.
++
++**Fix**: 
++1. Removed early returns for shift handling (lines 288-299)
