++# QuarterPro v3.2 Parity - Corrected Rounding Cliff Analysis
++
++**Date:** 2026-01-23  
++**Objective:** Fix rounding cliff analyzer to compute TRUE distance to flip boundary  
++**Result:** 3/12 passing, 0 rounding cliffs, 9 real mismatches
++
++---
++
++## Critical Fixes Applied
++
++### Fix #1: MPH Formatting Bug (STEP A)
++
++**Problem:** Float32 cast BEFORE banker's rounding broke tie-point behavior.
++
++**Evidence:**
++```
++160.85 as Float64: 160.85 (exactly at tie point)
++160.85 as Float32: 160.85000610351562 (slightly above tie, rounds up instead of to even)
++```
++
++**Solution:** Apply banker's rounding in Float64 space, not Float32.
++
++**File:** `src/domain/physics/vb6/vb6DisplayFormat.ts`
++- Removed Float32 cast before rounding for MPH
++- MPH value is already Float32 from vb6Exact trap calculation
++- Banker's rounding operates on that Float32 value in Float64 precision
++
++**Verification:** All tie-point tests now pass (16/16 in vb6.rounding.tie-behavior.spec.ts)
++
++### Fix #2: Rounding Cliff Analyzer (STEP B)
++
++**Problem:** Used guessed boundaries (0.005s, 0.05mph) instead of computing TRUE flip distance.
++
++**Old (wrong) logic:**
++```typescript
++const boundary = expectedValue + 0.005; // WRONG - doesn't account for banker's rounding
++const delta_raw = rawET - boundary;
++```
++
++**New (correct) logic:**
++```typescript
++// Determine flip direction (up/down)
++// Compute exact flip boundary using banker's rounding rules
++// Account for even/odd target values (banker's rounding to even)
++const flipBoundary = computeExactBoundary(targetValue, flip_direction);
++const delta_to_flip = Math.abs(rawET - flipBoundary);
++```
++
++**Key insight:** Banker's rounding flip boundaries depend on whether target is even/odd:
++- Target 4.98 (even): boundary at 4.985 (exactly at midpoint)
++- Target 4.99 (odd): boundary at 4.985 + epsilon (must exceed midpoint to previous even)
++
