++## Implementation Details
++
++### STEP 1: Evidence - Summary MPH is 66-ft Trap Speed
++
++**Source:** `src/domain/physics/models/vb6Exact.ts` lines 1092-1097, 1465-1472, 1506-1513
++
++**VB6 Formula:**
++```
++mph = 45.0 / dt
++where:
++  dt = t_finish - t_save
++  45.0 = 66 * 3600 / 5280 (exact constant)
++  t_save = time at 594 ft (eighth) or 1254 ft (quarter)
++  t_finish = time at 660 ft (eighth) or 1320 ft (quarter)
++```
++
++**Float32 Precision:** All trap calculations use Single (Float32):
++- `saveTime` cast to f32 when recorded
++- `interpolatedTrackTime` cast to f32 for trap calculation
++- `dt` computed as f32
++- `mph` result is f32
++
++**Documentation:** `docs/parity/quarterpro_v32_summary_mph_evidence.md`
++
++### STEP 2: Single Source of Truth Extractor
++
++**File:** `src/domain/physics/vb6/quarterProOutput.ts`
++
++**Interface:**
++```typescript
++export interface QuarterProSummary {
++  finishFt: number;
++  et_raw_s: number;
++  mph_raw: number;
++  et_display: string;
++  mph_display: string;
++  debug: QuarterProDebug;  // Trap calculation verification
++}
++```
++
++**Features:**
++- Extracts ET and MPH from timeslip entries at 660/1320 ft
++- Verifies trap calculation by recomputing from trap start times
++- Provides debug info showing t_save, t_finish, dt, mph_formula
++- Applies VB6 display formatting pipeline
