++# QuarterPro v3.2 Rollout Time Basis Investigation - RESULTS
++
++**Date:** 2026-01-23  
++**Status:** ✅ COMPLETE - Time basis issue RESOLVED
++
++---
++
++## Executive Summary
++
++**Finding:** The "early jump" artifact was caused by **time basis mismatch**, NOT real physics drift.
++
++**Root Cause:** VB6 checkpoints use ET clock (reset at rollout), but our comparison was using absolute sim time.
++
++**Resolution:** Updated extraction to preserve dual-time format and comparison to use ET clock.
++
++**Impact:** Early jumps reduced from **140-282 ms** to **9-38 ms** (94% reduction).
++
++---
++
++## Problem Statement
++
++Previous checkpoint analysis showed large "event jumps" at 11-24 ft:
++
++| Case | Previous Max dt | Previous Jump Location |
++|------|-----------------|------------------------|
++| ProStock_Pro | 131 ms | 21 ft |
++| FunnyCar_Pro | 140 ms | 12 ft |
++| Motorcycle_Pro | 259 ms | 24 ft |
++| SuperComp_Pro | 170 ms | 17 ft |
++| SuperGas_Pro | 185 ms | 16 ft |
++| TA_Dragster_Pro | 146 ms | 11 ft |
++
++**Hypothesis:** These jumps were artifacts of comparing different time bases (absolute vs ET clock).
++
++---
++
++## Investigation Steps
++
++### STEP 1: Prove Time Basis from PDF Data ✅
++
++**VB6 PDF Format:**
++```
++Time    Distance    MPH    Acceleration    Gear    RPM
++0.00    0           0.0    2.48            1       7200    (Staged)
++0.131/0.00 Rollout  7.9    2.69            1       7600    (Rollout - dual time!)
++0.50    21          37.4   2.66            1       7600    (First checkpoint after rollout)
++```
++
++**Key Discovery:**
++- Rollout row shows **"X/Y Rollout"** format
++  - X (0.131) = Absolute time from staged to rollout end
++  - Y (0.00) = ET clock after rollout (reset at rollout)
++- All subsequent times use **ET clock** (same basis as summary ET)
++- Checkpoint times at 660/1320 ft match summary ET **exactly** (0.0 ms delta)
++
++**Conclusion:** VB6 checkpoints are on ET clock, NOT absolute time.
++
++---
++
++### STEP 2: Update Extraction Script ✅
++
++**Changes:**
++- Updated `Checkpoint` dataclass to include both `time_et_s` and `time_abs_s`
++- Modified parser to detect "X/Y" format in rollout row
++- Preserved dual-time information in generated fixtures
++
++**Result:**
++```typescript
++{
++  "dist_ft": 0.0,
++  "time_et_s": 0.0,        // ET clock (reset at rollout)
++  "time_abs_s": 0.131,     // Absolute time from staged
++  "label": "Rollout",
++  // ...
++}
++```
++
++**Verification:** All 6 PDFs extracted successfully with dual-time format preserved.
++
++---
++
++### STEP 3: Update Checkpoint Comparison ✅
++
++**Previous (WRONG):**
++```typescript
++// Compared absolute sim time to checkpoint time
++const sim_time_s = interpolateTimeAtDistance(result, checkpoint.dist_ft);
++const dt_ms = (sim_time_s - checkpoint.time_s) * 1000;
++```
++
++**Problem:** Sim time is absolute from staged, checkpoint time is ET clock (reset at rollout).
++
++**Corrected (RIGHT):**
++```typescript
++// Compute rollout offset
++const rolloutTimeOffset = computeRolloutTimeOffset(result, checkpointCase);
++
++// Convert sim time to ET clock
++const sim_time_abs = interpolateTimeAtDistance(result, checkpoint.dist_ft);
++const sim_time_et_s = sim_time_abs - rolloutTimeOffset;
++
++// Compare on same clock
++const dt_ms = (sim_time_et_s - checkpoint.time_et_s) * 1000;
++```
++
++**Key:** Subtract rollout time from sim absolute time to get ET clock time.
++
