++# Trace Normalization Fix - Complete
++
++**Date:** 2025-01-27  
++**Issue:** VB6 equivalence debug report showed MPH=0.0 for all sim checkpoints  
++**Root Cause:** Trace schema/field mapping bug (not physics)  
++**Status:** ✅ FIXED
++
++---
++
++## Problem
++
++The VB6 equivalence debug report generator was showing:
++- MPH: 0.0 for all checkpoints
++- RPM: Incorrect values
++- Silent failures (defaulting to 0 instead of throwing errors)
++
++This was a **trace schema mismatch**, not a physics issue. The comparison code expected field names like `time_s`, `accel_g` but the classic sim runner trace used `time_et_s`, `accel`.
++
++---
++
++## Solution
++
++### 1. Created Trace Normalization Layer
++**File:** `src/integration-tests/helpers/vb6_trace_normalize.ts` (150+ lines)
++
++**Key Functions:**
++- `normalizeTraceRow(rawRow)` - Convert raw trace row to canonical format
++- `normalizeTrace(rawTrace)` - Normalize entire trace array
++- `validateTrace(trace)` - Regression assertions for trace validity
++- `printTraceStructure(rawTrace, label)` - Debug utility to inspect trace schema
++
++**Canonical Format:**
++```typescript
++interface NormalizedTraceRow {
++  time_s: number;
++  dist_ft: number;
++  mph: number;
++  rpm: number;
++  gear: number;
++  accel_g: number;
++}
++```
++
++**Field Name Support:**
++- **Time:** `time_et_s`, `time_s`, `time`, `t`
++- **Distance:** `dist_ft`, `distance_ft`, `dist`, `distance`, `d`
++- **Speed:** `mph`, `speedMph`, `vel_mph`, `vel_fps` (converts fps→mph)
++- **RPM:** `rpm`, `engineRpm`, `EngRPM`
++- **Gear:** `gear`, `currentGear`, `Gear`
++- **Accel:** `accel`, `accel_g`, `acceleration_g`, `AGS_g`
++
++**Error Handling:**
++- Throws descriptive errors if required fields cannot be found
++- Lists available keys in error message
++- No silent defaults to 0
++
++### 2. Updated VB6 Equivalence Debug Tool
++**File:** `src/integration-tests/helpers/vb6_equivalence_debug.ts`
++
++**Changes:**
++- `extractShiftEvents()` - Now normalizes trace before processing
++- `extractIntermediateSignals()` - Now normalizes trace before processing
++- `compareCheckpoints()` - Now normalizes trace before processing
++- `generateVB6EquivalenceReport()` - Added trace validation and optional debug output
++
++### 3. Added Regression Assertions
++**Function:** `validateTrace(trace)`
++
++**Checks:**
++- ✅ Trace is not empty
++- ✅ Final distance > 1200ft
++- ✅ Final speed > 50mph
++- ✅ No negative mph values
++- ✅ Distance is monotonically increasing
++
++**Behavior:** Throws descriptive errors if validation fails
++
++### 4. Added Debug Instrumentation
++**Function:** `printTraceStructure(rawTrace, label)`
++
++**Output:**
++- Trace length
++- Available field names
++- First row (JSON)
++- Middle row (JSON)
++- Last row (JSON)
++
++**Usage:** Enable in test with `debugTrace: true` parameter
++
++---
++
