++## Step 2: VB6 Semantics Verification ✅ COMPLETE
++
++### All 6 Trigger Types Implemented
++
++Based on VB6 TIMESLIP.FRM lines 815-1681 and manual QJR3W.txt:
++
++1. **STAGED** (initial conditions)
++   - VB6: TIMESLIP.FRM line 1059
++   - Emitted at t=0, d=0, v=0
++
++2. **ROLLOUT** (timing clock start)
++   - VB6: TIMESLIP.FRM lines 1373-1381
++   - ET reset, overhang adjustment
++
++3. **DISTANCE TRIGGERS** (30, 60, 330, 660, 1000, 1320 ft)
++   - VB6: TIMESLIP.FRM lines 815-818, 1295-1310
++   - Interpolation: sub310 (linear time/vel, exact distance)
++   - Factor^0.7 for AGS/RPM (sub325)
++
++4. **TIME INTERVAL TRIGGERS** (multiples of TimePrintInc)
++   - VB6: TIMESLIP.FRM lines 902-918, 1314-1320
++   - Selection: z = ET / TimePrintInc + 2 * (NGR - 1), choose smallest where z < kd
++   - kd = 28 (Quarter Jr), 33 (Quarter Pro)
++   - Interpolation: sub315 (linear dist/vel, exact time)
++
++5. **SPEED TRIGGERS** (60 mph, 100 mph)
++   - VB6: TIMESLIP.FRM line 818, 1425-1430
++   - First crossing events (0-60, 0-100 timing)
++   - Interpolation: velocity match (linear)
++
++6. **GEAR CHANGE TRIGGERS** (two rows per shift)
++   - VB6: TIMESLIP.FRM lines 1328-1342 (pre), 1440-1459 (post)
++   - Pre-shift: old gear at shift RPM
++   - Post-shift: new gear at reduced RPM
