++# VB6 TIMESLIP Print Formatting Analysis
++
++## VB6 Source: TIMESLIP.FRM lines 1490-1518
++
++### Print Format Rules
++
++```vb6
++Work = Vel(L) * Z5                           ' Z5 = 0.681818 (fps to mph)
++zr = Round(EngRPM(L), 10)                    ' Round RPM to nearest 10
++
++If iDist = 1 Then  ' Rollout row
++    Mid(prtline, 2, 20) = RightAlign(4, 3, time(L)) & "/0.00 Rollout"
++Else               ' Checkpoint rows
++    Mid(prtline, 3, 6) = RightAlign(5, 2, time(L))      ' Time: 2 decimals
++    Mid(prtline, 13, 5) = RightAlign(5, 0, Dist(L))     ' Distance: 0 decimals (integer)
++End If
++
++Mid(prtline, 22, 5) = RightAlign(4, 1, Work)            ' MPH: 1 decimal
++Mid(prtline, 32, 4) = RightAlign(3, 2, AGS(L))          ' Accel: 2 decimals
++Mid(prtline, 42, 1) = RightAlign(1, 0, zigr)            ' Gear: integer
++RSet zrRPM = Format(zr, "#,000")                        ' RPM: formatted with commas
++Mid(prtline, 45, 6) = zrRPM
++```
++
++### Formatting Summary
++
++| Field | VB6 Format | Decimals | Notes |
++|-------|------------|----------|-------|
++| time_s (rollout) | RightAlign(4, 3, ...) | 3 | Only for rollout row |
++| time_s (checkpoint) | RightAlign(5, 2, ...) | 2 | Standard checkpoints |
++| distance_ft | RightAlign(5, 0, ...) | 0 | Integer only |
++| mph | RightAlign(4, 1, ...) | 1 | Vel * 0.681818 |
++| accel_g | RightAlign(3, 2, ...) | 2 | AGS value |
++| gear | RightAlign(1, 0, ...) | 0 | Integer |
++| rpm | Round(..., 10) | N/A | Nearest 10, then formatted |
++
++---
++
