++# VB6 Rollout Bug Analysis and Fix
++
++## Problem Statement
++
++**Symptom:** QuarterProTest1 rollout checkpoint shows:
++- Expected (VB6): mph=7.9, rpm=7600
++- Actual (TS): mph=0.0, rpm=7200
++
++**Root Cause:** vb6Exact.ts detects rollout and starts the timer (line 1575) but **does not record the rollout checkpoint values** at that moment.
++
++## VB6 Source Evidence
++
++**TIMESLIP.FRM Lines 1379-1381:**
++```vb6
++Case 1:     DistTol = 0.1
++            If gc_Rollout.Value > 0 Then time(L) = 0
++            Dist(L) = Dist(L) + ovradj
++```
++
++**TIMESLIP.FRM Lines 1493-1519 (Printing rollout):**
++```vb6
++If iDist = 1 Then
++    Mid(prtline, 2, 20) = RightAlign(4, 3, time(L)) & "/0.00 Rollout"
++Else
++    Mid(prtline, 3, 6) = RightAlign(5, 2, time(L))
++    ...
++End If
++
++Mid(prtline, 22, 5) = RightAlign(4, 1, Work)  ' Work = Vel(L) * Z5 (mph)
++Mid(prtline, 32, 4) = RightAlign(3, 2, AGS(L))
++...
++zigr = iGear
++Mid(prtline, 42, 1) = RightAlign(1, 0, zigr)
++
++RSet zrRPM = Format(zr, "#,000")  ' zr = Round(EngRPM(L), 10)
++Mid(prtline, 45, 6) = zrRPM
++```
++
++**Key Insight:** VB6 prints rollout using **current state values** at the moment rollout is detected:
++- `Vel(L) * Z5` = current velocity in mph
++- `Round(EngRPM(L), 10)` = current engine RPM rounded to nearest 10
++- `AGS(L)` = current acceleration
++- `iGear` = current gear
++
++These are the values **after** the car has traveled rolloutFt distance, NOT the values at t=0 launch.
++
++## Current vb6Exact.ts Implementation
++
++**Lines 1566-1584 (Rollout detection):**
++```typescript
++if (timerStartTime_s === null) {
++  const DistStep = Math.abs(rolloutFt - state.Dist_ft);
++  const DistTol = 0.005;
++  const TimeTol = 0.002;
++  
++  if (DistStep < DistTol && (DistStep / state.Vel_ftps) < TimeTol) {
++    timerStartTime_s = state.time_s;  // Timer starts
++    state.Dist_ft = state.Dist_ft + ovradj;  // Add overhang
++    state.Dist0_ft = state.Dist_ft;
++    
++    console.log(`[vb6Exact] ROLLOUT: t=${timerStartTime_s.toFixed(4)}s, ...`);
++  }
++}
++```
++
++**Problem:** After setting `timerStartTime_s`, there's **no code** to record the rollout checkpoint with current mph/rpm/accel values.
++
++## Fix Required
++
++Add rollout checkpoint recording immediately after `timerStartTime_s = state.time_s`:
++
++```typescript
++if (DistStep < DistTol && (DistStep / state.Vel_ftps) < TimeTol) {
++  timerStartTime_s = state.time_s;
++  state.Dist_ft = state.Dist_ft + ovradj;
++  state.Dist0_ft = state.Dist_ft;
++  
++  // VB6 TIMESLIP.FRM:1493-1519 - Record rollout checkpoint
++  // Capture current state values at rollout completion
++  const rolloutMph = state.Vel_ftps * FPS_TO_MPH;
++  const rolloutRpm = Math.round(state.EngRPM / 10) * 10;  // VB6: Round(EngRPM(L), 10)
++  const rolloutAccel = state.AGS_g;
++  const rolloutGear = state.Gear;
++  
++  // Add to trace with special rollout marker
++  trace.push({
++    t_s: 0,  // ET = 0 at rollout
++    s_ft: 0,  // Track distance = 0 at rollout
++    v_fps: state.Vel_ftps,
++    v_mph: rolloutMph,
++    a_g: rolloutAccel,
++    rpm: rolloutRpm,
++    gear: rolloutGear,
++    isRollout: true,  // Special marker
++    rolloutAbsTime_s: timerStartTime_s,  // Absolute time at rollout
++  });
++  
++  console.log(`[vb6Exact] ROLLOUT: t_abs=${timerStartTime_s.toFixed(4)}s, mph=${rolloutMph.toFixed(1)}, rpm=${rolloutRpm}, gear=${rolloutGear}`);
++}
++```
++
++## Comparison Logic Fix
++
++The equivalence harness must recognize the rollout checkpoint (distance_ft=null in JSON) and compare it against the trace row with `isRollout: true` flag, NOT against the first trace row (which is at t=0 launch).
++
++**Current bug:** Harness likely compares rollout checkpoint against trace[0] which has mph=0, rpm=7200 (launch values).
++
++**Fix:** Find trace row with `isRollout: true` flag and compare against that.
++
++## Expected Results After Fix
++
++**Rollout checkpoint:**
++- mph: ~7.9 (velocity after traveling 8.5ft with ~2.5g accel)
++- rpm: 7600 (rounded to nearest 10)
++- accel: ~2.69g
++- gear: 1
++- time_et: 0.00s (by definition)
++- time_abs: ~0.13s (time to travel rolloutFt)
++
++This should match VB6 JSON expected values exactly.
