++# VB6 TIMESLIP.FRM Logic Analysis
++
++**Source:** `/Reference Files/OtherRefFiles/QPro Family 1_18_2023/QCommon/TIMESLIP.FRM`
++
++## Critical Findings for Rollout and Checkpoint Recording
++
++### 1. ROLLOUT CAPTURE (iDist=1)
++
++**VB6 Lines 1379-1381:**
++```vb6
++Case 1:     DistTol = 0.1    'reduced from .25 - 07/11/99
++            If gc_Rollout.Value > 0 Then time(L) = 0
++            Dist(L) = Dist(L) + ovradj    'adjust for front overhang
++```
++
++**VB6 Lines 1493-1494 (Printing):**
++```vb6
++If iDist = 1 Then
++    Mid(prtline, 2, 20) = RightAlign(4, 3, time(L)) & "/0.00 Rollout"
++```
++
++**Key Behaviors:**
++1. **When rollout is detected** (Dist ≈ DistToPrint(1) = rolloutFt):
++   - VB6 resets `time(L) = 0` (ET timer starts)
++   - VB6 adjusts `Dist(L) = Dist(L) + ovradj` (front overhang adjustment)
++   - VB6 captures **current state values**: `Vel(L)`, `EngRPM(L)`, `AGS(L)`, `Gear(L)`
++   
++2. **Rollout row values are NOT at t=0 launch:**
++   - mph = `Vel(L) * Z5` at rollout completion (NOT 0)
++   - rpm = `Round(EngRPM(L), 10)` at rollout completion (NOT launch RPM)
++   - These are the values **after** the car has traveled rolloutFt distance
++
++3. **Display format:** `"absolute_time/0.00 Rollout"`
++   - First number is absolute time from launch to rollout
++   - Second number is always 0.00 (ET starts at rollout)
++
++### 2. CHECKPOINT DETECTION
++
++**VB6 Lines 1296-1310:**
++```vb6
++VelDistMatch = 0:   DistStep = Abs(DistToPrint(iDist) - Dist(L))
++If DistStep < DistTol And (DistStep / Vel(L)) < TimeTol Then
++    PrintFlag = 1
++Else
++    If Dist(L) > DistToPrint(iDist) Then
++        Work = 3 * PQWT * (DistToPrint(iDist) - Dist(L)) + Vel(L) ^ 3
++        If Work > 0 Then VelDistMatch = Work ^ (1 / 3)
++```
++
++**Logic:**
++1. If within tolerance (`DistStep < DistTol` AND `DistStep/Vel < TimeTol`), print current values
++2. If overshot checkpoint, calculate `VelDistMatch` to revise velocity backward
++3. This triggers interpolation to hit exact checkpoint distance
++
++### 3. DISTANCE INTERPOLATION (sub310)
++
++**VB6 Lines 1609-1640:**
++```vb6
++Private Sub sub310()     'DISTANCE INTERPOLATION
++    factor = factor1
++    time(L) = Time0 + factor * (ASV(1) - Time0)
++    Dist(L) = DistToPrint(iDist)
++    Vel(L) = Vel0 + factor * (ASV(3) - Vel0)
++    
++    Select Case iDist
++        Case 3:     TIMESLIP(1) = time(L)   '60 ft
++        Case 4:     TIMESLIP(2) = time(L)   '330 ft
++        ...
++    End Select
++    
++    sub325
++End Sub
++
++Private Sub sub325()     'COMMON INTERPOLATION AND PRINT
++    factor = factor ^ 0.7
++    AGS(L) = Ags0 + factor * (ASV(4) - Ags0)
++    EngRPM(L) = RPM0 + factor * (ASV(6) - RPM0)
++    Gear(L) = ASV(7)
++```
++
++**Interpolation Method:**
++1. Linear interpolation for `time`, `Dist`, `Vel`
++2. **Non-linear** interpolation for `AGS` and `EngRPM`: `factor = factor ^ 0.7`
++3. Sets `Dist(L) = DistToPrint(iDist)` exactly
++4. Interpolates other values between saved state (ASV) and current state
++
++### 4. ROUNDING RULES
++
++**VB6 Line 1491:**
++```vb6
++zr = Round(EngRPM(L), 10)
++```
++
++**Display Rounding:**
++- RPM: Rounded to nearest 10 using VB6 `Round(value, 10)`
++- MPH: Displayed with 1 decimal place
++- Time: Displayed with 2 decimal places
++- Accel: Displayed with 2 decimal places
++
++**VB6 Round() behavior:**
++- `Round(value, increment)` in VB6 means round to nearest multiple of increment
++- Example: `Round(7583, 10) = 7580`, `Round(7587, 10) = 7590`
++- This is "round half away from zero" for the increment
++
++### 5. DISTANCE ARRAY (DistToPrint)
++
++**VB6 Lines 815-817 (Quarter Pro/Jr):**
++```vb6
++DistToPrint(1) = gc_Rollout.Value / 12: If DistToPrint(1) = 0 Then DistToPrint(1) = 1
++DistToPrint(2) = 30:        DistToPrint(3) = 60:        DistToPrint(4) = 330:      DistToPrint(5) = 594
++DistToPrint(6) = 660:       DistToPrint(7) = 1000:      DistToPrint(8) = 1254:     DistToPrint(9) = 1320
++```
++
++**Checkpoints for Quarter Pro/Jr:**
++1. Rollout (8.542ft for 102.5" rollout)
++2. 30ft
++3. 60ft
++4. 330ft
++5. 594ft (intermediate, not printed in some cases)
++6. 660ft
++7. 1000ft
++8. 1254ft (intermediate)
++9. 1320ft (1/4 mile)
++
