++## KEY TECHNICAL ACHIEVEMENTS
++
++### 1. Closest-Match Fallback for Provenance
++**Problem:** VB6 expects 21ft checkpoint, but emitter produces 20ft due to physics differences.
++
++**Solution:** When exact distance match is missing, find closest checkpoint within 2ft tolerance:
++```typescript
++if (!actual && typeof expected.distance_ft === 'number') {
++  const DISTANCE_TOLERANCE = 2; // ft
++  const candidates = formattedActual.filter(a => 
++    a.distance_ft !== null && 
++    Math.abs(a.distance_ft - expected.distance_ft) <= DISTANCE_TOLERANCE
++  );
++  if (candidates.length > 0) {
++    actual = candidates.reduce((closest, curr) => {
++      const closestDiff = Math.abs(closest.distance_ft! - expected.distance_ft);
++      const currDiff = Math.abs(curr.distance_ft! - expected.distance_ft);
++      return currDiff < closestDiff ? curr : closest;
++    });
++  }
++}
++```
++
++**Result:** Provenance from 20ft row (which has debug) is used for 21ft packet, preserving real interpolation data.
++
