++## 6. Offline / PWA Considerations
++
++### What to Cache (Service Worker)
++
++| Resource | Strategy | Why |
++|---|---|---|
++| App shell (HTML/CSS/JS) | Cache-first | Core app works offline |
++| Sim engine code (WASM/JS) | Cache-first | Sims run offline |
++| Saved vehicles (IndexedDB) | Local-first, sync on reconnect | Users can edit vehicles offline |
++| Saved sim projects (IndexedDB) | Local-first, sync on reconnect | Users can run sims offline |
++| Last known capabilities | localStorage | UI gating works offline |
++| Track database | Cache-first, refresh weekly | Track list for offline sim setup |
++
++### What NOT to Allow Offline
++
++| Action | Why | UX |
++|---|---|---|
++| Billing / checkout | Requires Stripe | Show "Requires internet connection" |
++| Admin actions | Must be server-verified | Hide admin nav when offline |
++| User registration / login | Requires Clerk | Show "Sign in when online" |
++| Library install (shared assets) | Requires server | Show "Available when online" |
++| Run history sync | Requires server | Queue locally, sync on reconnect |
++
++### Sync Strategy
++
++1. **Optimistic local writes:** Vehicles and sim projects save to IndexedDB immediately.
++2. **Background sync:** When online, a service worker syncs pending changes to the server.
++3. **Conflict resolution:** Last-write-wins with timestamp comparison. If server has newer data, prompt user.
++4. **Capability refresh:** On reconnect, fetch `/api/capabilities.php` and compare `capability_version`. If changed, update local cache and re-render.
++
++### UX: Messaging Offline Limitations
++
++- **Offline banner:** Subtle top bar: "You're offline — sims and saved data work, billing and sync paused."
++- **Disabled buttons:** Billing, admin, and sync buttons show a tooltip: "Requires internet connection."
++- **Pending sync indicator:** Small badge on nav showing "3 changes pending sync."
++
