++# Step Trace Workflow for VB6 Parity Analysis
++
++This document describes how to generate and compare step-level traces between the TypeScript simulation and VB6 reference implementation.
++
++## Overview
++
++Step traces capture the simulation state at each "converged velocity step" - the point where VB6's iteration loop has converged (TIMESLIP.FRM line 1278). This is:
++- **AFTER** the convergence loop (lines 1244-1276)
++- **BEFORE** trigger/print checks (lines 1279+)
++
++Comparing traces at this exact point allows identification of the first divergence in physics calculations.
++
++## Generating TS Step Traces
++
++### 1. Enable Step Trace Capture
++
++Set the environment variable before running tests:
++
++```bash
++export RSA_STEP_TRACE=1
++npm test -- vb6_equivalence --run
++```
++
++Or programmatically:
++
++```typescript
++import { setStepTraceCapture } from '../domain/physics/vb6/vb6SimulationStep';
++setStepTraceCapture(true);
++```
++
++### 2. Run Simulation
++
++The step trace data is captured in the `stepTrace` field of each `VB6StepComputed` result.
++
++### 3. Write Traces to CSV
++
++Use the step trace writer to output CSV:
++
++```typescript
++import { writeStepTraceCsv, StepTraceRow } from './tools/step_trace_writer';
++
++// Collect step traces during simulation
++const traces: StepTraceRow[] = [];
++// ... run simulation, collect stepResult.stepTrace for each step ...
++
++// Write to file
++const csv = writeStepTraceCsv('QuarterProTest1', traces);
++fs.writeFileSync('reports/step_traces/ts/QuarterProTest1.csv', csv);
++```
++
++## Generating VB6 Step Traces
++
++### 1. Instrument VB6
++
++Follow the instructions in `docs/VB6_INSTRUMENTATION.md` to add trace output to TIMESLIP.FRM.
++
++### 2. Run VB6 Simulation
++
++Run the desired test case in VB6. The instrumented code will output `step_trace.csv`.
++
++### 3. Copy Trace to Reports Directory
++
++```bash
++cp /path/to/vb6/step_trace.csv reports/step_traces/vb6/QuarterProTest1.csv
++```
++
++## Comparing Traces
++
++### Using diff_first_divergence.ts
++
++```bash
++npx ts-node src/integration-tests/tools/diff_first_divergence.ts --case QuarterProTest1
++```
++
++Output example:
++```
++================================================================================
++FIRST DIVERGENCE REPORT: QuarterProTest1
++================================================================================
++
++Step Index: 42
++Number of divergent fields: 2
++
++DIVERGENT FIELDS:
++--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
++  Field: accel_g
++    VB6 Block: acceleration_clamp
++    VB6 Value: 0.892345
++    TS Value:  0.891234
++    Delta:     0.001111
++    Tolerance: 0.00001
++
++  Field: HP_after_losses
++    VB6 Block: hp_chain
++    VB6 Value: 245.67
++    TS Value:  245.12
++    Delta:     0.55
++    Tolerance: 0.01
++
++--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
++
++NEXT STEPS:
++  1. Open VB6 TIMESLIP.FRM and locate the block(s) listed above
++  2. Compare the exact formula/precedence/clamps in VB6 vs TS
++  3. Port the VB6 logic exactly to TS
++  4. Re-run this diff to verify the divergence moves later
++  5. Document the fix in PARITY_REPORT.md with VB6 line references
++```
++
++## Trace CSV Schema
++
++| Column | Description | VB6 Variable |
++|--------|-------------|--------------|
++| stepIndex | Step counter | L |
++| time_abs_s | Absolute time from launch | time(L) |
++| time_et_s | ET after rollout | time(L) - RolloutTime |
++| dt_s | Timestep used | TimeStep |
++| dist_abs_ft | Absolute distance | Dist(L) |
++| dist_track_ft | Track distance | Dist(L) - ovradj |
++| vel_fps | Velocity in ft/s | Vel(L) |
++| vel_mph | Velocity in mph | Vel(L) * Z5 |
++| accel_g | Acceleration in g's | AGS(L) |
++| gear | Current gear | Gear(L) |
++| engine_rpm | Engine RPM | EngRPM(L) |
++| driveshaft_rpm | Driveshaft RPM | DSRPM |
++| HP_raw | HP from curve | HPSave/ClutchSlip |
++| HP_after_clutch | HP after clutch/converter | HPSave |
++| HP_after_losses | HP after all losses | HP |
++| TQ_lbft | Engine torque | Z6*HP/RPM |
++| clutchSlip | Clutch/converter slip | ClutchSlip |
++| torqueMult | Torque multiplier | gc_TorqueMult.Value |
++| slipRatio | Converter slip ratio | SlipRatio |
++| tireForce_lbf | Force at tire | force |
++| dragForce_lbf | Total drag force | DragForce |
++| rollRes_lbf | Rolling resistance | cmu1*DownForce |
++| netForce_lbf | Net force | force-DragForce |
++| rearWeight_lbf | Dynamic rear weight | DynamicRWT |
++| frontWeight_lbf | Dynamic front weight | DynamicFWT |
++| tractionLimit_g | Traction limit | AMAX |
++| CRTF | Traction coefficient | CRTF |
++| tireSlip | Tire slip factor | TireSlip |
++| slip_flag | Traction limited flag | SLIP(L) |
++| shift_flag | Shift state | ShiftFlag |
++| PQWT | Power/weight term | PQWT |
++| k_iterations | Convergence iterations | k |
++
++## Field Tolerances
++
++| Category | Fields | Tolerance | Rationale |
++|----------|--------|-----------|-----------|
++| Exact | stepIndex, gear, shift_flag | 0 | Must match exactly |
++| Time | time_abs_s, time_et_s, dt_s | 1e-6 | High precision |
++| Position | dist_*, vel_* | 1e-4 | Tight tolerance |
++| Acceleration | accel_g | 1e-5 | Critical for parity |
++| Power | HP_*, TQ_* | 0.01 | Power chain |
++| Forces | *Force_lbf, *Weight_lbf | 0.1 | Force calculations |
++| Slip | clutchSlip, slipRatio, tireSlip | 1e-5 | Drivetrain |
++
++## VB6 Block Attribution
++
++When a divergence is found, the tool reports which VB6 code block the field belongs to:
++
++| Block | VB6 Lines | Description |
++|-------|-----------|-------------|
++| loop_control | 1078-1082 | Step counter, timestep |
++| timestep_calc | 1082 | Adaptive timestep |
++| clutch_converter_calc | 1144-1173 | EngRPM, ClutchSlip, SlipRatio |
++| hp_curve_lookup | 1176-1178 | TABY call |
++| drag_calc | 1180-1194 | Wind, DragForce, DragHP |
++| weight_transfer | 1196-1211 | DynamicFWT, DynamicRWT |
++| traction_calc | 1213-1216 | CAXI, CRTF, AMax |
++| hp_chain | 1218-1229 | TGEff, Efficiency, TireSlip |
++| acceleration_clamp | 1260-1266 | AGS reflection/clamping |
++| convergence_loop | 1244-1276 | Iteration, PQWT, time |
++| distance_calc | 1280 | Dist(L) calculation |
++| trigger_logic | 1295-1355 | Distance/time/speed/shift triggers |
++
++## Troubleshooting
++
++### No Trace Output
++
++1. Verify `RSA_STEP_TRACE=1` is set
++2. Check that `setStepTraceCapture(true)` is called before simulation
++3. Verify the simulation completes without errors
++
++### Trace Length Mismatch
++
++If VB6 and TS have different numbers of steps:
++- Check timestep calculation (TSMax, adaptive formula)
++- Verify velocity revision logic (VelDistMatch, VelTimeMatch, etc.)
++- Check shift handling (DTShift, ShiftFlag)
++
++### Large Divergence at Step 1
++
++Early divergence often indicates:
++- Different initial state (Ags0, force calculation)
++- Different HP curve generation
++- Different torque multiplier calculation
