++# VB6 Step Trace Instrumentation
++
++This document describes how to instrument VB6 TIMESLIP.FRM to output step traces for parity comparison with the TypeScript implementation.
++
++## Overview
++
++The step trace captures the simulation state at the exact point VB6 defines as "CONVERGED VELOCITY STEP" (line 1278). This is:
++- AFTER the inertia transient convergence loop (lines 1240-1276)
++- BEFORE the print/trigger checks (lines 1279+)
++
++## Instrumentation Steps
++
++### 1. Add File Handle Declaration
++
++At the top of the `Timeslip` subroutine (around line 500), add:
++
++```vb
++Dim hTraceFile As Integer
++Dim TraceFilePath As String
++```
++
++### 2. Open Trace File
++
++After the initialization section (around line 1000, before the main loop), add:
++
++```vb
++' Open step trace file for parity analysis
++TraceFilePath = App.Path & "\step_trace.csv"
++hTraceFile = FreeFile
++Open TraceFilePath For Output As #hTraceFile
