++## Float32 Precision Analysis
++
++VB6 uses Single (32-bit float) for most calculations. However, we should NOT blindly apply Float32 everywhere.
++
++**VB6 Type Boundaries:**
++- Variables declared as `Single` should be truncated to Float32 at assignment
++- Intermediate calculations may use higher precision
++- Integer operations (like ShiftRPM) should NOT use Float32
++
++**Current Float32 Usage:**
++- `f(x)` - Converts to Float32 if useFloat32 is true
++- `M.add/sub/mul/div` - Float32 arithmetic operations
++- `M.sqrt/pow/abs` - Float32 math functions
++
++**Potential Issues:**
++1. Over-application of Float32 in intermediate calculations
++2. Missing Float32 at actual VB6 assignment boundaries
++3. Integer values being incorrectly converted to Float32
++
