++## 1. VB6 Type Rules (from VB6 Language Reference)
++
++| Declaration Pattern | Resulting Type | Example |
++|---------------------|----------------|---------|
++| `Public Const X = 3.14` | **Double** | No suffix = Double |
++| `Const X = 3.14` | **Double** | No suffix = Double |
++| `Const X! = 3.14` | **Single** | `!` suffix = Single |
++| `Const X# = 3.14` | **Double** | `#` suffix = Double |
++| `Dim Y As Single` | **Single** | Explicit declaration |
++| `Dim Y As Double` | **Double** | Explicit declaration |
++| Numeric literal `0.96` | **Double** | No suffix = Double |
++| Numeric literal `0.96!` | **Single** | `!` suffix = Single |
++
++**VB6 Expression Evaluation Rule:**
++- If ANY operand in an expression is Double, the ENTIRE expression is evaluated in Double precision.
++- Truncation to Single occurs ONLY at assignment to a Single variable.
++
