++## 7. Summary: VB6 Coercion Pattern
++
++**Pattern for EVERY INIT statement:**
++1. RHS expression is evaluated in **Double** (because at least one operand is Double - usually a constant or CValue)
++2. Result is truncated to **Single** ONLY at the assignment boundary
++3. No intermediate truncation occurs within the expression
++
++**TS Implementation Rule:**
++```typescript
++// VB6: HP = gc_HPTQMult.Value * HP / hpc
++// RHS: Double * Single / Single → evaluated in Double
++// Assignment: truncate to Single
++const HP = vb6AssignSingle(vehicle.HPTQMult * HP_raw / hpc);
++```
