++## 6. Issues Found and Fixed
++
++### 6.1 TABY Bracket Expansion Logic (FIXED)
++
++**Issue:** The T200/T300 control flow in `dtaby.ts:187-194` was incorrect.
++
++**VB6 Logic (RSALIB.BAS:548-556):**
++```vb
++T200:   'DETERMINE PROPER VALUES OF KBOTM% AND KTOP%
++    If JJ% = 1 Or L% <= 1 Then GoTo T400      ' Skip expansion if boundary or linear
++    KTOP% = KTOP% + 1                          ' Expand upper
++    If L% >= 3 Then GoTo T300                  ' If cubic+, always go to T300
++    If KTOP% <= N% Then GoTo T400              ' If L=2 and KTOP still valid, done
++
++T300:
++    If KTOP% > N% Then KTOP% = N%              ' Clamp KTOP
++    KBOTM% = KBOTM% - 1                        ' Expand lower
++    If KBOTM% < 1 Then KBOTM% = 1              ' Clamp KBOTM
++```
++
++**Old TS (WRONG):**
++```ts
++if (L >= 3 || KTOP > N - 1) {  // BUG: condition conflates two cases
++```
++
++**New TS (CORRECT):**
++```ts
++if (L >= 3) {
++  // T300: expand both directions
++  if (KTOP > N - 1) KTOP = N - 1;
++  KBOTM = KBOTM - 1;
++  if (KBOTM < 0) KBOTM = 0;
++} else {
++  // L = 2 (quadratic)
++  if (KTOP > N - 1) {
++    // KTOP exceeded limit, must expand lower instead
++    KTOP = N - 1;
++    KBOTM = KBOTM - 1;
++    if (KBOTM < 0) KBOTM = 0;
++  }
++  // else: KTOP is valid, go to T400
++}
++```
++
++**VB6 Anchor:** RSALIB.BAS:548-556
++
++### 6.2 Duplicate Implementations (DOCUMENTED)
++
++**Issue:** `vb6Interpolation.ts` contains a complete duplicate of TABY/BISC/DTABY with 1-indexed arrays.
++
++**Resolution:** Keep `vb6Interpolation.ts` for legacy engine code that expects 1-indexed arrays. Document that `dtaby.ts` is the canonical 0-indexed implementation for simulation code.
++
++**Canonical Module:** `src/domain/physics/vb6/dtaby.ts`
++
++### 6.3 YVAL Truncation in TABY (ACCEPTABLE)
++
++**VB6 Behavior:** `YVAL = YVAL + P` truncates to Single on each iteration because YVAL is `As Single`.
++
++**TS Behavior:** `taby()` computes entirely in Double and returns Double. Caller is responsible for truncation.
++
++**Analysis:** This is semantically correct because:
++- VB6 TABY is called with YVAL ByRef, and the caller's variable determines truncation
++- TS returns a value that the caller truncates with `vb6AssignSingle()` if needed
++- TIMESLIP.FRM uses L=1 (linear, 2 points), so only one iteration of the outer loop occurs
++
++**Status:** Acceptable. For L=1 (the common case), there's only one P value, so no accumulation truncation occurs.
++
