++## 6. Float32 Truncation Points (Critical for Parity)
++
++### Init Calculation Chain
++```
++HP_launch = TABY(...)           → f() truncation
++HP_corrected = HP * mult / hpc  → M.div(M.mul(...)) truncation at each op
++TQ = Z6 * HP / RPM              → M.div(M.mul(...)) truncation at each op
++TQ = TQ * mult * TGR * TGEff    → M.mul(...) chain truncation
++force = TQ * GR * Eff / (slip * dia / 24) - drag  → M.sub(M.div(...))
++Ags0 = factor * force / Weight  → M.div(M.mul(...))
++CRTF = CAXI * AX * dia * (width+1) * (...)  → M.mul(...) chain
++AMax = (CRTF - drag) / Weight   → M.div(M.sub(...))
++```
++
++### Integer Coercions
++- `iGear` (gear index): Integer in VB6, number in TS
++- `L` (step counter): Integer in VB6, number in TS
++- `iDist` (distance print index): Integer in VB6, number in TS
++- `iMPH` (speed print index): Integer in VB6, number in TS
++
++### Rounding Points
++- `vb6Round(value, increment)` for printed output
++- `Math.fround()` for all intermediate Single values
++- VB6 `Int()` vs JS `Math.floor()` for integer truncation
++
