++## UI Sanity Checklist (VB6 vs RSA side-by-side)
++
++Quick visual checks a developer should verify when comparing VB6 Engine Pro and RSA:
++
++1. **Flow Details chart** — X axis ticks match VB6 (may be non-45° steps when IVO < TDC). Left Y axis does NOT use RoundUp. Curves clip at axis bounds (`allowDataOverflow`), not at data bounds.
++2. **Flow Bench lift/flow columns** — Lift shows 3 decimals (e.g., `0.100`), flow shows 1 decimal. FV Index shows 1 decimal. Chart X axis uses lift values with 1-decimal ticks; Y axes match VB6 RoundUp scaling.
++3. **Mech Details 15-row table** — Includes the AngMPS row (angle of max piston speed, ~73°). Depth shows 3 decimals, speed shows 0 decimals. Chart tooltip uses VB6 formatting.
++4. **Flow Details cam overrides** — Duration and Max Valve Lift inputs highlight blue when overridden. Hover tooltip shows base value and allowed range. Reset button (↩) shows the base value. Overrides affect table + chart + axis seeds but NOT the main engine config.
++5. **Dyno chart + data table** — Expand the collapsible table below the chart. RPM/HP/TQ values in the table should match the chart curve points exactly. HP and TQ are integers (VB6 rounds to whole numbers).
++6. **Performance card** — Peak HP, Peak TQ, Displacement, HP/CID, TQ/CID all use VB6 banker's rounding (`vb6Fixed`). Shift and Redline RPM are integers rounded to nearest 50.
