++### engFileParser.ts — ❌ BROKEN Detail
++
++The TS parser at `src/domain/physics/engine/engFileParser.ts` is fundamentally broken:
++
++**Problem 1: Hardcoded values** (lines 70-76):
++```ts
++  const inline = 1;  // V-engine (most common)
++  const camType = 4;  // Normal Flat Tappet & Solid Lifter (from BASECASE)
++  const carb = true;  // Carburetor (from BASECASE)
++  const deltaP = 28;  // Standard flowbench pressure
++```
++These 4 fields are hardcoded to BASECASE defaults instead of being read from the file.
++
++**Problem 2: No version branching.** VB6 `LoadFromFile` has 4 version branches:
++```vb
++' ECommon/ENGINE.FRM lines 2111-2162
++    If ver = "3" Or ver = "3.0.1" Or ver = "3.1" Then
++        Input #ff, inline, ncyl, ibore, istroke, rod, CR
++        Input #ff, ctype, indur, ifi, carb, ifuel
++        ...
++    Else
++        ' Version "2" — completely different field order
++        Input #ff, ncyl, ibore, istroke, rod, CR, carb, iman
++        Input #ff, niv, pif, inh2o, refbor, flowf, ctype, indur
++        ...
++```
++The TS parser ignores version entirely.
++
++**Problem 3: Wrong field order.** The TS parser assumes a line-per-group format that doesn't match either VB6 version branch.
++
