++## Top Gaps — VB6-Execution-Order Priority
++
++Strictly follows VB6 runtime initialization order. No impact-based reordering.
++
++1. **❌ cValue semantics** — `Value` setter auto-clamp + `IsChanged` gate + `Formatted`/`ValFmt`. Foundation for all other gaps. VB6: `Cvalue.CLS:46–72, 334–341, 419–423`.
++2. **❌ SetAllValues** — Initialize all field constraints (defaults, min/max, decimal places, AllowMM). VB6: `ENGPERF.BAS:1729+`.
++3. **❌ SetMinMax** — Foundation routine all setters depend on. VB6: `ENGPERF.BAS:1677–1727`.
++4. **❌ Dynamic clamp routines** — 20 `Set*`/`Test*` routines. Without these, users can enter physically impossible combinations. VB6: `ENGPERF.BAS:1312–1675`.
++5. **❌ Business rules** — Force-inline-for-odd-cyl, force-IR-for-1-cyl, round-cam-to-even. VB6: `ENGINE.FRM:1509–1522, 1966`.
++6. **❌ Conditional HP/TQ formatting** — Small engines (<100 HP) display wrong precision. VB6: `ENGINE.FRM:2030–2039`.
++7. **❌ .ENG file parser** — Current TS parser is **BROKEN** (hardcoded values, wrong field order, no version branching). VB6: `ENGINE.FRM:2070–2299`.
++8. **⚠️ CalcRecommendations** — ~400 lines, TS port exists at `engineProDetails.ts:calcRecommendations()` but unverified.
++9. **❌ Worksheets** — CR, Carb CFM, CSA worksheets not ported.
++10. **❌ Inch/mm auto-detect** — VB6 supports dual units; TS is inch-only.
