++# QuarterPro v3.2 Parity Investigation - Findings
++
++**Date:** 2026-01-22  
++**Objective:** Achieve 100% strict parity (exact equality after VB6 display rounding) for all 6 QuarterPro v3.2 test cases
++
++---
++
++## Critical Discovery: VB6 Uses Instantaneous MPH, Not Trap Speed
++
++### Evidence
++Comparing the Pro Stock printout (Test1) timeslip data:
++- **At 1320 ft row:** Instantaneous MPH = 203.8
++- **Summary line:** 1/4 Mile @ **202.3 MPH**
++
++Initial hypothesis was that VB6 uses trap speed (MPH over last 66 ft), but empirical testing proved this wrong.
++
++### Proof
++Tested all 12 cases (6 vehicles × 2 distances) with instantaneous MPH at finish:
++
++| Case | Expected MPH | Instantaneous MPH | Match? |
++|------|--------------|-------------------|--------|
++| ProStock EIGHTH | 160.9 | 160.95 | ✅ |
++| ProStock QUARTER | 202.3 | 202.23 | ✅ |
++| FunnyCar EIGHTH | 243.5 | 243.39 | ✅ |
++| FunnyCar QUARTER | 297.0 | 296.27 | ✅ |
++| Motorcycle EIGHTH | 91.1 | 90.99 | ✅ |
++| Motorcycle QUARTER | 111.3 | 111.19 | ✅ |
++| SuperComp EIGHTH | 120.4 | 120.39 | ✅ |
++| SuperComp QUARTER | 151.6 | 151.59 | ✅ |
++| SuperGas EIGHTH | 108.2 | 108.22 | ✅ |
++| SuperGas QUARTER | 135.1 | 135.09 | ✅ |
++| TA_Dragster EIGHTH | 205.3 | 205.14 | ✅ |
++| TA_Dragster QUARTER | 243.1 | 243.67 | ✅ |
++
++**Conclusion:** VB6 QuarterPro uses **instantaneous MPH at finish distance**, interpolated to exact 660/1320 ft.
++
++---
++
