++## Why 12/12 Strict Parity May Be Unattainable
++
++### Root Causes of Remaining Failures
++
++1. **Float32 vs Float64 Numeric Differences**
++   - VB6 uses Float32 (Single) throughout
++   - Our sim uses Float64 (Double) with `Math.fround()` conversions
++   - Accumulated over hundreds of integration steps → small drift
++
++2. **Banker's Rounding Cliffs**
++   - VB6 uses banker's rounding (round-half-to-even)
++   - Small numeric differences can cause display value to flip
++   - Example: 160.85 rounds to 160.8 (even) vs 160.9 (if slightly above tie)
++
++3. **Integration Method Subtleties**
++   - VB6 integration order/precision may differ subtly
++   - Our port is extremely close but not bit-identical
++   - Sub-millisecond differences accumulate
++
