++
++## E) Stability Risks & Duplications
++
++### Parallel Access Systems (HIGH)
++Three systems (legacy hasFeature, capabilities hasCap, subscription features) must agree.
++- **Risk:** Adding a new gated feature requires updating 3 places + guards.ts
++- **Mitigation:** Centralized guards, `useAccessDiagnostics()` hook, AccessSmokeTest panel, no-ad-hoc safety tests
++- **Consolidation direction:** Migrate everything to capabilities system; deprecate legacy hasFeature and subscription features over time
++
++### String-Literal Feature Gates (MEDIUM)
++`clutch_sim` is still used as a string literal in ProtectedRoute. Not yet centralized.
++- **Risk:** Typos, no compile-time safety, no diagnostics coverage
++- **Consolidation direction:** Add `CLUTCH_SIM_FEATURE` constant to guards.ts, same pattern as other gates
++
++### localStorage as Primary Storage (HIGH)
++Vehicles, runs, preferences, library assets all stored in localStorage.
++- **Risk:** Data loss on browser clear, no cross-device sync, 5MB limit
++- **Consolidation direction:** Add Clerk-backed remote storage or dedicated API; localStorage becomes cache layer
++
++### Legacy Route Aliases (LOW)
++`/parts`, `/events`, `/maintenance`, `/expenses` all redirect to TeamHub.
++- **Risk:** SEO confusion, maintenance burden
++- **Consolidation direction:** Replace with proper redirects or remove after migration period
++
++### Engine Sim Dual Layout (LOW)
++`/engine-sim` (new dashboard) and `/engine-sim-legacy` (old three-column) coexist.
++- **Risk:** Maintenance of two UIs for same feature
++- **Consolidation direction:** Remove legacy layout once dashboard is feature-complete
++
++### No Backend API (HIGH)
++All data is client-side. No server for sync, sharing, or team features.
++- **Risk:** Team features are limited to single-device, no real collaboration
++- **Consolidation direction:** Build lightweight API (Clerk webhooks + DB) for vehicle/run sync
++
