++/**
++ * Regression Guard: No Per-Op Truncation in VB6 Production Code
++ * 
++ * This test scans VB6-path production files and fails if it finds:
++ * - M.* usage (per-operation Float32 math)
++ * - f( usage (per-operation Float32 wrapper)
++ * 
++ * These patterns violate VB6 semantics which compute in Double and truncate
++ * only at assignment to Single variables.
