++ * This suite validates 100% strict VB6 parity (exact equality after VB6 display rounding)
++ * for QuarterPro v3.2 ET + MPH against the 6 legacy printouts.
++ * 
++ * Source of truth: QuarterPro v3.2 PDF printouts
++ * - Test1: Pro Stock (prostock.dat)
++ * - Test2: Funny Car (funnycar.dat)
++ * - Test3: Motorcycle (motorcyc.dat)
++ * - Test4: Super Comp (supercmp.dat)
++ * - Test5: Super Gas (supergas.dat)
++ * - Test6: TA Dragster (tadrag.dat)
++ * 
++ * CRITICAL: VB6 printouts have a known gear labeling bug where gears start at "2nd"
++ * with no "1st" shown. The simulation DOES start in 1st gear. Configs have been
++ * corrected to map printout "2nd" → actual 1st, "3rd" → actual 2nd, etc.
++ * 
++ * Test approach:
++ * - Use VB6Exact model (exact VB6 TIMESLIP.FRM replication)
++ * - Apply VB6 display rounding (roundET/roundMPH) for parity
++ * - Assert strict equality (no tolerance) on rounded ET/MPH
++ * - Validate timeslip increments exist and are properly ordered
++ */
