++/**
++ * Deep investigation of QuarterPro MPH values.
++ *
++ * VB6 uses TWO different mph pipelines:
++ * 1. "Printed row" mph: instantaneous velocity Vel(L) * Z5 at each distance checkpoint
++ *    - This is what appears in the VB6 run trace / PDF output
++ *    - Computed from physics state at the exact distance target (with sub310 interpolation)
++ * 2. "Timeslip" mph at 660ft and 1320ft: trap speed = 66ft / Δtime
++ *    - 660ft trap: 66 / (time@660 - time@594)
++ *    - 1320ft trap: 66 / (time@1320 - time@1254)
++ *    - This is the "official" ET slip mph
++ *
++ * TS mirrors this exactly:
